Z||000000||burdell1||03-22-2000||11:13 AM||||Has anyone out there tried to replace the speakers in the headrest with new ones? Is it very hard to do? I was planning on replacing the seat covers and thought I could replace the headrest speakers with some better quality tweeters....||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spyder||03-22-2000||11:25 AM||||Here you go: <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com/addspeakers.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mrmikes.com/addspeakers.htm</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com/faq.htm#getspeakers" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mrmikes.com/faq.htm#getspeakers</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||coyote||03-22-2000||01:12 PM||||I have actuallly replaced them in my 84, i did when i recovered the seats. If you are carefull you can remove the upper seat cover, and replace them. I used 3 1/2" coaxials. the head rest is pretty forgiving and it is a easy swap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||03-22-2000||05:32 PM||||Headrest speakers give mediocre sound quality at best.  And I hope you're short.  Otherwise your speakers will be driving into your shoulders instead of your ears.  If you really want a good sound, either do the work and put speakers in the sail panels or use separates in the front and forget about the rear speakers alltogether (except for something small for rear fill)&gt;||||reg||1
